  "review": {
    "review": "The hero remained alive at 56/75 HP when the planner exhausted its options. Decisions 3681-3682 selected and fired an identified, noncursed magic-missile staff at the only observed actor, a DM-100. The accepted transition at log line 10575 consumed one charge and advanced one turn: level 11 with 56/60 XP became level 12 with 2/65 XP, exactly six earned XP. Arcane Vision was already learned, yet no DM-100 remained in the subsequent public observation. The old receipt required adjacency, unchanged level and complete neighborhood visibility, so it missed this ranged level-up kill. Remembered lightning exposure then blocked preparation, pickup, recovery and exploration at decision 3683 (line 10576). Source inspection supports a focused new receipt using consumed charge, a clear observed projectile ray, Arcane Vision tracking and exact XP rollover; disappearance alone remains insufficient. A reduced public-evidence regression failed two assertions on original source and passed on the candidate. All 1,961 Python tests passed, with four skipped. Only targeting/receipt bookkeeping was reconstructed; original full runtime memory and individual rejected door routes were not recovered. The correction does not certify a replacement movement or future success. Policy and new regression changes are supplied through the trusted change adapter; files is intentionally empty.",
    "learnings": "A ranged magic-missile kill can cross a hero level boundary without fresh defeat text. Retire only the matching lightning memory when charge consumption, an observed clear ray, Arcane Vision and exact six-XP rollover jointly confirm the kill. Preserve ambiguity checks, unfinished pickups and terminal exhaustion rather than manufacturing waits."
